	"note": "Seed 709787393. Nightly sweep (attachment clean-ups). A device, offline, queued a setBlob whose blob another device's GC then swept (unreferenced, past the grace) before the frame committed; its file had moved on, so the R3 gate found the blob in neither the store nor local bytes and sent the frame anyway. It revived a doc deleted elsewhere pointing at a missing blob, and every device retried the download forever. Fix: blobs/touch.ts withdraws such an ns frame (context.ts dropUnsent) and the planner re-derives the doc from the disk. Focused test: touch.test.ts \"an ns frame whose blob is gone everywhere is withdrawn\".",
